# Kessler

## Overview

Kessler is an orbital demolition arcade game played in the browser. A planet
sits at the center of the field, circled by three rings of derelict satellites
and junk clusters slated for demolition. The player rides the deflector around
a low track above the planet, batting a demolition ball outward into the
rings, and sweeping the derelicts from the sky is the cleanup itself. A
breaking derelict may shed a salvage pod, and a caught pod grants the
deflector a tool. A ball the deflector misses burns up against the planet.

Play is a score attack over endless waves. Clearing every derelict refills the
rings for the next wave, faster and worth more, and the run ends when the last
ball is lost with no lives left. The strong player steers the bounce, because
where the ball meets the deflector decides the angle it leaves at.

Kessler ships the art and the sound it plays, and this build makes them. The
planet and pod sprites, the ball's spin frames, the particle systems, and the
game's cues and music are produced during the build with the asset-generation
binaries on the `PATH`, committed to the repository, and bundled by the build.
`specs/assets.md` is that contract.

Kessler has its own name, look, and rules, and its assets, branding, and
design are original to it.

