### The build interface

`npm ci` followed by `npm run build` produces the complete static site into
`dist/` at the repository root, with an `index.html` at the root of that
directory as the entry point. That directory runs correctly when served as-is,
both at the root of a static file server and mounted under a sub-path, so
every URL the build emits or constructs at runtime is page-relative rather
than root-absolute. The scripts that do this are already in `package.json`.

The build is self-contained. The asset tools on this machine's `PATH` are
development tools for producing the files `specs/assets.md` lists and locates;
the produced files are committed, the build bundles them, and neither `npm ci`
nor `npm run build` invokes a tool.

## Goal of this build

Produce a complete, polished, playable game that runs entirely in a browser,
and the art and sound it plays. This is a substantial build: a deflector
orbiting a planet, three counter-rotating rings of derelicts, five kinds of
salvage pod, endless waves, six screens, and a produced set of sprites,
particle systems, and sounds. Aim for a game a person would enjoy playing,
where a bounce goes where it was steered.

### Hard requirements

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
- Write the runtime the game stands on: the frame loop and its delta time, the
  canvas fit, keyboard input, image loading, audio with looping beds, and the
  debug overlay.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
- Build on the {{engine.name}} engine, taking the frame loop, the input
  actions, audio with looping beds, asset loading, the canvas fit, and the
  debug overlay from it.
{{else}}
- Build on the {{engine.name}} engine, taking the frame loop, rendering, the
  input actions, audio with looping beds, asset loading, the canvas fit, and
  the debug overlay from it, and writing the game inside its framework of game
  modes, actors, components, and controllers.
{{/if}}
- Render real graphics on the canvas. A text-only or character-cell rendering
  does not meet this.
- Produce the sprites, particle systems, cues, and music during this build,
  commit the produced files, and bundle them. `specs/assets.md` states what to
  produce, how each file is made, and how it is wired in.
- Run in the browser with no backend. Everything needed to play is
  self-contained, and no API key or credential is needed to build, run, or
  play.
- Replace the starter `README.md` with one explaining what the game is, how to
  install dependencies, how to run it in development, how to produce the
  static production build, and the controls.

